[{:db/id "q-49206/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "8afd4198-41eb-5684-af29-1523fceb95fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49206/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "ee26fc1e-31f0-56bc-8bfa-cc970beb02d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49206/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" :answer/id #uuid "9a6c630f-a465-58dc-b7f4-eca8d3851383" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49206/selection/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e" :answer/id #uuid "537bdde3-b02a-5a7e-91d5-dc508c1c30b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49206/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" :answer/id #uuid "e798e2f6-3045-5934-9b47-f421e52efb21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49206/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2c123162-227f-5a83-9cf7-7153866e7bca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49206/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a" :answer-field/choices ["q-49206/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-49206/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-49206/selection/f7ec98ce0d2d5e0413aaea93f098b04337f2217a14eff2f5b611bfb2fc659059" "q-49206/selection/4c919dd28b6dc49158e4bc0cd4ecb2267c6fa1a0cbd5673af1ca376ab1c8a23e" "q-49206/selection/cca93330bdc2ff0543861ebace1767f4dbf656d494475323c839b42f25a3876a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-49206" :question/id #uuid "df468f4e-2d83-51ff-a604-abd18e09aab6" :question/math-academy-id "q-49206" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/22472e04f7bd26076da43a2ad17a192726ad19b5bd3885ce066c9523cad4f870.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of three parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-2,-1],$ the line segment for $x\\in (-1,1),$ and the line segment for $x\\in (1,3].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={{{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,-1].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle. Therefore, we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-1.5.\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-1,1).$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+3)(2) \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (1,3].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+2)(2) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =-1.5+5+3 \\\\  & =6.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49206/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-49206"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174/selection/ac05fbca7d414e58584a3dd32efd2f68cd7c6e24f0b9af84927d3ee9d08a61f7" :answer/id #uuid "97255af8-a483-51c4-80e3-0129d7413bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174/selection/3b4a7e747d90751ea7ac3e251ecbcc52cb0c3c2a9a51ca324675615c67208734" :answer/id #uuid "4909127d-d3ef-50aa-9e10-a02ce28169eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174/selection/dd32444b4e386b9afc6b269a80de329441f33f906b76f7dd67166157dd01bb38" :answer/id #uuid "cccd6aab-30ef-5d1e-b5c2-16056043112d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174/selection/35ed9501ec5b62a7ed24d688fe6b06d37e655a56b304b49f7153e4cd1c78da7d" :answer/id #uuid "bdbdddce-6bb9-5d6f-bd08-be7557a8f000" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174/selection/b644519198c5577ee9c67d3c2bda34509dad7578583bd4b906c108e9348c2cb4" :answer/id #uuid "77f0a833-75df-5102-8814-f868d63b9f87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2014b57f-2aff-53dd-89c9-a9eda5d5e635" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-86174/selection/dd32444b4e386b9afc6b269a80de329441f33f906b76f7dd67166157dd01bb38" :answer-field/choices ["q-86174/selection/ac05fbca7d414e58584a3dd32efd2f68cd7c6e24f0b9af84927d3ee9d08a61f7" "q-86174/selection/3b4a7e747d90751ea7ac3e251ecbcc52cb0c3c2a9a51ca324675615c67208734" "q-86174/selection/dd32444b4e386b9afc6b269a80de329441f33f906b76f7dd67166157dd01bb38" "q-86174/selection/35ed9501ec5b62a7ed24d688fe6b06d37e655a56b304b49f7153e4cd1c78da7d" "q-86174/selection/b644519198c5577ee9c67d3c2bda34509dad7578583bd4b906c108e9348c2cb4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-86174" :question/id #uuid "6f31c4e7-003d-5a6c-9983-dff54f594d65" :question/math-academy-id "q-86174" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/3e0eca1a04396c0c86bbf5c3e5a9b3ff7071eacfe3d8c4281549e70cda809e8c.png)\n\nGiven the graph of $y=f(x)$ above, find the value of \n${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-2,3)$ and the arc of the quarter-circle for $x\\in (3,5].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,3).$ The corresponding region is a right triange, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (3,5].$ The corresponding region is a combination of an inverted quarter-circle of radius $2$ and a square, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & ={s}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =4-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =5+(4-\\pi ) \\\\  & =9-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-86174/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86174"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316261/field-1/f3838c56a8eb889c1f6f2b36f16f743fa0a93501d8266c6eb9e0d7112c099f90" :answer/id #uuid "c18aa5b7-c992-5b32-a357-5e724ba96bd5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9+\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316261/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4170770-80a0-5c01-a8a3-394cfa36e747" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316261/field-1/f3838c56a8eb889c1f6f2b36f16f743fa0a93501d8266c6eb9e0d7112c099f90" :answer-field/choices ["q-316261/field-1/f3838c56a8eb889c1f6f2b36f16f743fa0a93501d8266c6eb9e0d7112c099f90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316261" :question/id #uuid "f14565cc-b995-5571-b40e-c5bb6b6d3c35" :question/math-academy-id "q-316261" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/d36f2859865da58d226a738d8338f726df950db75b7421b604bb692c9049d54a.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The graph consists of $2$ parts: the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-4,-2]$ and the line segment for $x\\in (-2,1].$ So, we can use the additive property of integrals to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-2].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot (1)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (-2,1].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2+1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi +9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316261/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316261"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-338507/field-1/45f9c68d67f50b9d07653a9516f81d087414425a489a338a6744afb5b50241f3" :answer/id #uuid "d0bf7010-3f64-5b22-8fc4-82fc0116c4ef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338507/field-1/eaee83082a78997b354789e1a4932b1c30bf776d280f39b0b58686ce5df99b0a" :answer/id #uuid "eabd0215-ed94-5435-bebd-84d0f8f97cc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "17.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338507/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "603a54c5-8911-5f08-b53b-a8d967ee08be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338507/field-1/45f9c68d67f50b9d07653a9516f81d087414425a489a338a6744afb5b50241f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-338507/field-1/45f9c68d67f50b9d07653a9516f81d087414425a489a338a6744afb5b50241f3" "q-338507/field-1/eaee83082a78997b354789e1a4932b1c30bf776d280f39b0b58686ce5df99b0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338507" :question/id #uuid "550da44a-dc56-593e-bbdf-dd12d1acd2aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-338507" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/8eb7c4fe147028c6dc31aad2427a33bb713553e610101b1fd263bda30f5c49d0.png)\n\nThe graph $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Then,\n\n${\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $4$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-6,-4],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-4,-3),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-3,0),$ and the line segment for $x\\in [0,5].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-6}^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{4}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-6,-4].$   The corresponding region is a triangle below the $x$-axis, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-6}^{-4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-3).$   The corresponding region is a triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,0).$   The corresponding region is a rectangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =bh \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,5].$   The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(3+1)(5) \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-6}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{1}{2}+6+10 \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338507/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4abe11e-febf-5461-96ee-bca8a7713bdf"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338507"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-353136/field-1/5b1da9f4fe6bb3c8c95b9a91e9ceb99cce98b1f62f5a8cc926c4f68bf6ce64ee" :answer/id #uuid "91204a75-1a83-5274-8195-9162d1e95fae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14-2\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-353136/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "630dbbfe-452a-5391-8ba4-f98903b06972" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-353136/field-1/5b1da9f4fe6bb3c8c95b9a91e9ceb99cce98b1f62f5a8cc926c4f68bf6ce64ee" :answer-field/choices ["q-353136/field-1/5b1da9f4fe6bb3c8c95b9a91e9ceb99cce98b1f62f5a8cc926c4f68bf6ce64ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-353136" :question/id #uuid "e3ea9770-cd37-54c4-9097-58e7386e8964" :question/math-academy-id "q-353136" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14032967/assets/f7eebd794b43da16658750db0df3a4d4c4b894ddb80f84795ea483aa4d579f56.png)\n\nIf the graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above, then\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We divide the interval of integration into $3$ regions: the arc of the semi-circle for $x\\in [-4,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in [0,4),$ and the line segment for $x\\in (4,6].$ Using the additive property of integrals, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}.\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,0].$ The corresponding region is a lower semi-circle of radius $2$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi (2)^{2} \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2\\pi .\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,4).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}4\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (4,6].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4+2)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =-2\\pi +8+6 \\\\  & =14-2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-353136/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb30dbbf-4f83-59d0-b712-f0e592aafb27"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-353136"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
